
# PENDING — this section is deliberately empty.
#
# featureAdd(ctx, f) mutates client._features, so a case would have to assert
# on the shared client that every other section also uses, and undo itself
# afterwards. The runner constructs one client per spec (DEF.client) rather
# than one per entry, so there is no isolation to build that on yet.
#
# An empty `set` runs ZERO cases. Runners must not treat that as a pass by
# accident: the language runners keep a PENDING list, and corpus.test.ts
# asserts that every empty fixture is declared there AND explains itself —
# so an accidentally-blanked fixture fails the build while a knowingly
# deferred one does not.

# Machine-readable so the corpus guard can check it; the prose above
# is the long form.
basic: pending: 'featureAdd mutates client._features; the runner builds one client per spec, not per entry, so a case cannot isolate or undo itself.'
basic: set: []
